         "source": [
            "import pandas as pd\n",
            "from sklearn import utils,preprocessing\n",
            "\n",
            "df=pd.read_csv('Clean_Dataset.csv')\n",
            "df=df.drop(columns='Unnamed: 0')\n",
            "df=utils.shuffle(df,random_state=1) # shuffling before splitting into training & evaluation (swl oumaima wsh blan tdar hadi wla la)\n",
            "\n"
         ]
      },
      {
         "cell_type": "markdown",
         "id": "b70a15b6",
         "metadata": {},
         "source": [
            "the columns (features) that should be encoded are:\n",
            "airline, flights, departure & arrival times, source & destination cities, stops, class\n",
            "\n",
            "the other ones are already numerical & don't need any more encoding (days_left, price, duration)\n",
            "\n",
            "i suppose all the data in here is relevant to use in the ML Training\n",
            "\n",
            "[doc for preprocessing](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/preprocessing.html#encoding-categorical-features)"
         ]
      },
      {
         "cell_type": "code",
         "execution_count": null,
         "id": "d44de303",
         "metadata": {},
         "outputs": [],
         "source": [
            "#### Preprocessing (Encoding) \n",
            "categorical_df=df[['airline','source_city','destination_city','days_left','arrival_time','departure_time']]\n",
            "encoder_cat=preprocessing.OneHotEncoder(sparse_output=False)\n",
            "array_encoded = encoder_cat.fit_transform(categorical_df)\n",
            "\n",
            "encoded_cat = pd.DataFrame(\n",
            "    array_encoded,\n",
            "    columns = encoder_cat.get_feature_names_out(categorical_df.columns)\n",
            ")\n",
            "encoded_cat"
         ]
      },
      {
